cat > room_tool/BRIEF.md <<'EOF'
# room_tool (Codex Astra): a head-backed program for room size, in the v3.14 runtime and generator, on CPU with tests
Your folder: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_cd/room_tool (write only here). Everything else is read-only: copy what you change into work/.

## Why
The student answers spatial questions by writing a short program that calls its own heads; the runtime computes from the heads' depth, pose and masks and prints values the model copies into its answer. Room size has no program today (rows answer directly). Lane gt_ceiling measured that a mask-free rule on predicted geometry beats direct answering on VSI-Bench room size by 12.4 points [+4.5, +21.2] (78.9 against 66.6, 76 items; out-of-sample rule choice survives): floor cells seen by at least two frames, voted, with the tower's pose and G3T depth. One benchmark task in eight, so about 1.5 points of the benchmark's task average. Build the program so that the next training leg can teach it.

## Inputs (read-only)
- Reference rule and its pricing: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_cd/gt_ceiling/work/tg/geomswap.py (the room floor-cell vote), work/tp/prog_v2.py (room label rule on ground truth; note the saved lesson that an older room rule read 12-23% high: use prog_v2's current rule), events/20261111T1632Z_RESULT_tower_geometry.md, 20261111T1638Z_RESULT_t6_1_oos_rule_choice.md, 20261111T1648Z_RESULT_t6_2_policy_selector_masks.md, and the executor port work/port/ (PORT_SPEC.md, V314_FUSION_POLICY.patch: geometry_mode sensor | predicted).
- The runtime and generator to extend: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_cd/integ_v314/work/tree_v314_r2 and work/gen_r2 (out/RECORD.md, events/20261111T1554Z_RESULT_integ_v314_pass2.md). The scene renderer's newest types as a pattern for a new type: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_cd/render_gaps/out/RENDER_GAPS.patch, PATCH_MAP.md, ROWS_READ_GAPS.md.
- Geometry exports for replay on this node: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_cd/ttower/work/geo/heads_g3s64 (G3T depth) and heads_g3s64_vcd; ground-truth rooms and scenes as gt_ceiling's code loads them.

## Build
1. The call. One new head call in the trace grammar, in the style of the existing ones (`<ground ...>`, `<angle ...>`, `<gap ...>`): the model asks for the floor area; the tool response prints what the answer needs and what a reader can check (the frames used, the floor height, the area in square metres to 2 decimals, and the count of floor cells or the bounding extents). Choose the form that changes the grammar least; write it in out/GRAMMAR.md with one worked example.
2. The runtime. In sensor mode (ground truth; trace generation) the value is prog_v2's label rule on the scene's ground truth, so training rows are exact; in predicted mode it is the floor-cell vote on the heads' depth and pose, matching geomswap.py (state every parameter: cell size, vote threshold, floor-height estimate, gravity source). Typed refusals (no floor seen, too few frames, NaN) that the caller turns into the direct-answer fallback; never a plausible wrong number.
3. The generator and scene renderer: a room-size row type in the benchmark's template (square metres), with the validator checks the other types have (exact replay, template, label equality within the type's tolerance, dev exclusion, token and gate positions, pack round trip).
4. Tests: sensor mode equals prog_v2's answer on every local ground-truth room (state n and mismatches); predicted mode reproduces gt_ceiling's priced numbers on its 76 VSI-Bench room items within 0.5 points (state both); the decoder parses what the generator writes, byte for byte; a 3.13 session refuses the new call; each refusal path.
5. Wording rule for every sentence the model is trained to write: state the computation; never mention a benchmark, dataset, label or release.

## Deliver
out/ROOM_TOOL.patch against tree_v314_r2 and gen_r2 (list the files), out/GRAMMAR.md, out/ROWS_READ_ROOM.md (8 rendered rows from 8 scenes chosen by a fixed seed, in the layout of render_gaps' ROWS_READ_GAPS.md, plus 3 refusals), out/PRICING.md (sensor parity, predicted-mode numbers against gt_ceiling's, per-item table path), events/<UTC stamp from date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%MZ>_RESULT_room_tool.md and a final message, each at most 15 lines.

## Limits
CPU only; no GPU, no ssh, no git commands, no network, no deletion commands of any kind. Run under `ulimit -f 204800`; folder under 2 GB; temporary files under work/tmp, not /tmp; at most 8 CPU threads. /home and /data* are overloaded network storage: do not read or write them. You cannot ask questions: decide, and write the choice down.
EOF
